#. Tag: title
#: developers-scripting.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scripting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In &krita;, you can write scripts in Ruby or Python (the availability of the "
"interpreters might depend on what your distributions or the administrator of "
"your machine did install). Here you will find a description of the scripting "
"API."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:9
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some examples are distributed with &krita;, and you might find them in "
"<filename>/usr/share/apps/krita/scripts</filename> (or <filename>/opt/kde/"
"share/apps/krita/scripts</filename>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: developers-scripting.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid "Variables in the <classname>Krosskritacore</classname> module"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<varname>KritaDocument</varname> returns a <classname>Document</classname> "
"object"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<varname>KritaScript</varname> returns a <classname>ScriptProgress</"
"classname> object"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can retrieve an object using the <function>get</function> function of "
"the <classname>Krosskritacore</classname> module, in Ruby you will have to "
"write something like that:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: developers-scripting.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"doc = Krosskritacore::get(\"KritaDocument\")\n"
"script = Krosskritacore::get(\"KritaScript\")"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: developers-scripting.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid "Functions in the <classname>Krosskritacore</classname> module"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getBrush</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function returns a <classname>Brush</classname> taken from the list of "
"&krita; resources. It takes one argument: the name of the brush. For example "
"(in Ruby):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: developers-scripting.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid "Krosskritacore::getBrush(\"Circle (05)\")"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getFilter</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function returns a <classname>Filter</classname> taken from the list of "
"&krita; resources. It takes one argument: the name of the filter. For "
"example (in Ruby):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: developers-scripting.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid "Krosskritacore::getFilter(\"invert\")"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getPattern</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function returns a <classname>Pattern</classname> taken from the list "
"of &krita; resources. It takes one argument: the name of the pattern. For "
"example (in Ruby):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: developers-scripting.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid "Krosskritacore::getPattern(\"Bricks\")"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>loadBrush</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function loads a <classname>Brush</classname> and then returns it. It "
"takes one argument: the filename of the brush."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>loadPattern</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function loads a <classname>Pattern</classname> and then returns it. It "
"takes one argument: the filename of the pattern."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>newCircleBrush</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function returns a <classname>Brush</classname> with a circular shape. "
"It takes at least two arguments: width and height. It can take two other "
"arguments: width of the shading, and height of the shading. If the shading "
"is not specified, no shading will be used. For example (in Ruby):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: developers-scripting.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Krosskritacore::newCircleBrush(10,20) # create a plain circle\n"
"Krosskritacore::newCircleBrush(10,20,5,10) # create a gradient"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>newHSVColor</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function returns a new <classname>Color</classname> with the given HSV "
"triplet. It takes three arguments: hue component (0 to 255), saturation "
"component (0 to 255), value component (0 to 255). For example (in Ruby):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: developers-scripting.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "Krosskritacore::newHSVColor(255,125,0)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>newImage</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function returns a new <classname>Image</classname>. It takes four "
"arguments: width, height, colorspace id, name of the image. And in return "
"you get an <classname>Image</classname> object. For example (in Ruby):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: developers-scripting.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "Krosskritacore::newImage(10,20, \"RGBA\", \"kikoo\")"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>newRectBrush</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function returns a <classname>Brush</classname> with a rectangular "
"shape. It takes at least two arguments: width and height. It can take two "
"other arguments: width of the shading and height of the shading. If the "
"shading is not specified, no shading will be used. For example (in Ruby):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: developers-scripting.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Krosskritacore::newRectBrush(10,20) # create a plain rectangle\n"
" Krosskritacore::newRectBrush(10,20,5,10) # create a gradient"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>newRGBColor</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function returns a new <classname>Color</classname> with the given RGB "
"triplet. It takes three arguments: red component (0 to 255), blue component "
"(0 to 255), green component (0 to 255). For example (in Ruby):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: developers-scripting.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Krosskritacore::newRGBColor(255,0,0) # create a red color\n"
"Krosskritacore::newRGBColor(255,255,255) # create a white color"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: developers-scripting.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Descriptions and function lists for various objects in "
"<classname>Krosskritacore</classname>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "Object: PaintLayer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>beginPainting</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>convertToColorspace</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Convert the image to a colorspace. This function takes one argument: the "
"name of the destination colorspace. For example (in Ruby):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: developers-scripting.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "image.convertToColorspace(\"CMYK\")"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>createHistogram</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function creates a Histogram for this layer. It takes two arguments: "
"the type of the histogram (\"RGB8HISTO\"), and 0 if the histogram is linear, "
"or 1 if it is logarithmic."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>createHLineIterator</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create an iterator over a layer, it will iterate on a row. This function "
"takes three arguments: <varname>x</varname> (start in the row), <varname>y</"
"varname> (vertical position of the row), width of the row."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>createPainter</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function creates a <classname>Painter</classname> which will allow you "
"to paint on the layer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>createRectIterator</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create an iterator over a layer, it will iterate on a rectangular area. This "
"function takes four arguments: <varname>x</varname>, <varname>y</varname>, "
"width of the rectangle, height of the rectangle."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>createVLineIterator</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create an iterator over a layer, it will iterate on a column. This function "
"takes three arguments: <varname>x</varname> (horizontal position of the "
"column), <varname>y</varname> (start in the column), height of the column."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>endPainting</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "This function closes the current undo entry and adds it to the history."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>fastWaveletTransformation</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "Returns the fast wavelet transformation of the layer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>fastWaveletUntransformation</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Untransforms a fast wavelet into this layer. It takes one argument: a "
"wavelet object. For example (in Ruby):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: developers-scripting.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"wavelet = layer.fastWaveletTransformation()\n"
"layer.fastWaveletUntransformation(wavelet)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getHeight</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Return the height of the layer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getWidth</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid "Return the width of the layer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid "Object: <classname>Filter</classname>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getFilterConfiguration</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function returns the <classname>FilterConfiguration</classname> "
"associated with this filter."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>process</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function will apply the filter. It takes at least one argument: the "
"source layer. You can also use these four arguments: <varname>x</varname>, "
"<varname>y</varname>, <varname>width</varname>, <varname>height</varname>. "
"(<varname>x</varname>,<varname>y</varname>,<varname>width</varname>,"
"<varname>height</varname>) defines the rectangular area on which the filter "
"will be computed. If the rectangle is not defined, then the filter will be "
"applied on the entire source layer. For example (in Ruby)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: developers-scripting.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"doc = Krosskritacore::get(\"KritaDocument\")\n"
"image = doc.getImage()\n"
"layer = image.getActivePaintLayer()\n"
"width = layer.getWidth()\n"
"height = layer.getHeight()\n"
"filter = Krosskritacore::getFilter(\"invert\")\n"
"filter.process(layer, layer)\n"
"filter.process(layer, layer, 10, 10, 20, 20 )"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid "Object: <classname>FilterConfiguration</classname>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getProperty</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function returns the value of a parameter of the associated "
"<classname>Filter</classname>. It takes one argument: the name of the "
"parameter."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setProperty</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function defines a parameter of the associated <classname>Filter</"
"classname>. It takes two arguments: the name of the parameter and the value, "
"whose type depends on the <classname>Filter</classname>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid "Object: <classname>Histogram</classname>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This class allows you to access the histogram of a <classname>PaintLayer</"
"classname>. Example (in Ruby):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: developers-scripting.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"doc = krosskritacore::get(\"KritaDocument\")\n"
" image = doc.getImage()\n"
" layer = image.getActiveLayer()\n"
" histo = layer.createHistogram(\"RGB8HISTO\",0)\n"
" min = layer.getMin() * 255\n"
" max = layer.getMax() * 255\n"
" for i in min..max\n"
"   print layer.getValue(i)\n"
"   print \"\\n\"\n"
" end"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getChannel</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid "Return the selected channel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getCount</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid "This function returns the number of pixels used by the histogram."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getHighest</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "This function returns the highest value of the histogram."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getLowest</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid "This function returns the lowest value of the histogram."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getMax</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function returns the maximum bound of the histogram (values at greater "
"position than the maximum are null). The value is in the range 0.0 &ndash; "
"1.0."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getMean</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid "This function returns the mean of the histogram."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getMin</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function returns the minimum bound of the histogram (values at smaller "
"position than the minimum are null). The value is in the range 0.0 &ndash; "
"1.0."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getNumberOfBins</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "Return the number of bins of this histogram."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getTotal</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid "This function returns the sum of all values of the histogram."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getValue</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Return the value of a bin of the histogram. This function takes one "
"argument: index, in the range [0..255]."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setChannel</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the channel of the layer on which to get the result of the histogram. "
"This function takes one argument: the channel number."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "Object: <classname>ScriptProgress</classname>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<classname>ScriptProgress</classname> is used to manage the progress bar of "
"the status bar in &krita;. For example (in Ruby):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: developers-scripting.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"script = Krosskritacore::get(\"KritaScript\")\n"
"script.setProgressTotalSteps(1000)\n"
"script.setProgressStage(\"progressive\", 0)\n"
"for i in 1..900\n"
"  script.incProgress()\n"
"end\n"
"script.setProgressStage(\"brutal\", 1000)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>incProgress</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "This function increments the progress by one step."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setProgress</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function sets the value of the progress. It takes one argument: the "
"value of the progress."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setProgressStage</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid "This function sets the value of the progress and displays the text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setProgressTotalSteps</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function set the number of steps that the script will require. It takes "
"one argument: the maximum value of the progress"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid "Object: <classname>Wavelet</classname>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This object holds the coefficients of a wavelet transformation of a "
"<classname>PaintLayer</classname>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:274
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getDepth</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:274
#, no-c-format
msgid "Returns the depth of the layer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getNCoeff</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns the value of the Nth coefficient. The function takes one argument: "
"the index of the coefficient."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getNumCoeffs</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns the number of coefficients in this wavelet (= size * size * depth)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getSize</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid "Returns the size of the wavelet (size = width = height)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getXYCoeff</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns the value of a coefficient. The function takes two arguments: "
"<varname>x</varname> and <varname>y</varname>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setNCoeff</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set the value of the Nth coefficient. The function takes two arguments: the "
"index of the coefficient and the new value of the coefficient."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setXYCoeff</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set the value of a coefficient. The function takes three arguments: "
"<varname>x</varname>, <varname>y</varname>, and the new value of the "
"coefficient."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid "Object: <classname>Painter</classname>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>convolve</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function applies a convolution kernel to an image. It takes at least "
"three arguments: a list of kernels (all lists need to have the same size), "
"factor, and offset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The value of a pixel will be given by the following function: K * P / factor "
"+ offset, where K is the kernel and P is the neighbourhood."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It can take the following optional arguments: <varname>borderOp</varname> "
"(control how to convolve the pixels on the border of an image: 0 = use the "
"default color, 1 = use the pixel on the opposite side of the image, 2 = use "
"the border pixel, 3 = avoid border pixels), <varname>channel</varname> (1 "
"for color, 2 for alpha, 3 for both), <varname>x</varname>, <varname>y</"
"varname>, <varname>width</varname>, <varname>height</varname>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setFillThreshold</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sets the fill threshold. It takes one argument: the threshold."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>fillColor</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Starts filling with a color. It takes two arguments: <varname>x</varname> "
"and <varname>y</varname>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>fillPattern</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Starts filling with a pattern. It takes two arguments: <varname>x</varname> "
"and <varname>y</varname>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>paintPolyline</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function will paint a polyline. It takes two arguments: a list of x "
"positions, and a list of y positions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>paintLine</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function will paint a line. It takes five arguments: <varname>x1</"
"varname>, <varname>y1</varname>, <varname>x2</varname>, <varname>y2</"
"varname>, and <varname>pressure</varname>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>paintBezierCurve</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function will paint a Bezier curve. It takes ten arguments: "
"<varname>x1</varname>, <varname>y1</varname>, <varname>p1</varname>, "
"<varname>cx1</varname>, <varname>cy1</varname>, <varname>cx2</varname>, "
"<varname>cx2</varname>, <varname>x2</varname>, <varname>y2</varname>, "
"<varname>p2</varname>, where (<varname>x1</varname>,<varname>y1</varname>) "
"is the start position, <varname>p1</varname> is the pressure at the start, "
"(<varname>x2</varname>,<varname>y2</varname>) is the end position, "
"<varname>p2</varname> is the pressure at the end. (<varname>cx1</varname>,"
"<varname>cy1</varname>) and (<varname>cx2</varname>,<varname>cy2</varname>) "
"are the positions of the control points."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>paintEllipse</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function will paint an ellipse. It takes five arguments: <varname>x1</"
"varname>, <varname>y1</varname>, <varname>x2</varname>, <varname>y2</"
"varname>, <varname>pressure</varname>, where (<varname>x1</varname>,"
"<varname>y1</varname>) and (<varname>x2</varname>,<varname>y2</varname>) are "
"the positions of the two centers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:362
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>paintPolygon</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:362
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function will paint a polygon. It takes two arguments: a list of x "
"positions and a list of y positions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>paintRect</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function will paint a rectangle. It takes five arguments: <varname>x</"
"varname>, <varname>y</varname>, <varname>width</varname> <varname>height</"
"varname>, <varname>pressure</varname>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>paintAt</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function will paint at a given position. It takes three arguments: "
"<varname>x</varname>, <varname>y</varname>, <varname>pressure</varname>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setPaintColor</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function sets the paint color (also called foreground color). It takes "
"one argument: a <classname>Color</classname>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setBackgroundColor</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function sets the background color. It takes one argument: a "
"<classname>Color</classname>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setPattern</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function sets the pattern used for filling. It takes one argument: a "
"<classname>Pattern</classname> object."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setBrush</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function sets the brush used for painting. It takes one argument: a "
"<classname>Brush</classname> object."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setPaintOp</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function defines the paint operation. It takes one argument: the name "
"of the paint operation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setDuplicateOffset</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function defines the duplicate offset. It takes two arguments: the "
"horizontal offset and the vertical offset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setOpacity</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function set the opacity of the painting. It takes one argument: the "
"opacity, in the range 0 to 255."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setStrokeStyle</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function sets the style of the stroke. It takes one argument: 0 for "
"none, or 1 for brush."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setFillStyle</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function sets the fill style of the <classname>Painter</classname>. It "
"takes one argument: 0 for none, 1 for fill with foreground color, 2 for fill "
"with background color, 3 for fill with pattern."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid "Object: <classname>Iterator</classname>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This object allows you to change pixel values one by one. The name of some "
"functions depends on the colorspace, for instance, if the colorspace of the "
"layer is RGB, you will have <function>setR</function>, <function>setG</"
"function> and <function>setB</function>, and for CMYK: <function>setC</"
"function>, <function>setM</function>, <function>setY</function> and "
"<function>setK</function>. In the documentation below we will assume that "
"the colorspace is called ABC, with three channels: A, B and C."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Functions: <function>setA</function>, <function>setB</function>, "
"<function>setC</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:427
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Those functions take one argument: the new value of one of the channels of "
"this pixel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>setABC</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set the value of all channels. This function takes one argument: an array "
"with the new values for all channels."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:435
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Functions: <function>getA</function>, <function>getB</function>, "
"<function>getC</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid "Return the value of one of the channels of this pixel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>getABC</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid "Return an array with the values of all channels."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:442
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>darken</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:442
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Darken a pixel. This function takes at least one argument: <varname>shade</"
"varname> (amount used to darken all color channels). This function can take "
"the following optional argument: <varname>compensation</varname> (to limit "
"the darkening)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:448
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>invertColor</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:448
#, no-c-format
msgid "Invert the color of a pixel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:451
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>next</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:451
#, no-c-format
msgid "Increment the position, go to the next pixel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:454
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function: <function>isDone</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-scripting.docbook:454
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Return true if the iterator is at the end (no more pixels are available)."
msgstr ""

